{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04V2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{G}_m$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\begin{itemize}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:07ec336e81d7d31a39e8e5247bcb23d0c81f9f298cf8701d626739a99ef71149", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d987c0beb4805fe9242f01268d49c3dd9575a408e86d1f8332a6b6486da01cb4", "source_text": "Rigidification is a process for removing a flat subgroup from the inertia. For example, if <MATH_0001> is a projective variety, the morphism from the Picard stack to the Picard scheme is a rigidification of the group of automorphism <MATH_0002>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3a42206c0309e507d4d0be9ffcbbe4ff9ff01bb64f4f45a957a7b7c79e9e7bd3", "unit_id": "tag:04V2:p001"}
